# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: clal-load-aldo-configuration-not-hermetic — a no-UI test failed on the persistent macOS runner
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -

* Symptom

=test:clautolisp:macos= failed (job 16466188513, MR !192 pipeline 2843757118)
with a single failing check in =AUTOLISP-BUILTINS-CORE-SUITE=:

: CLAL-UI-AND-DEBUG-BUILTINS-RETURN-NIL-WITHOUT-A-UI
:   (clal-load-aldo-configuration) should return nil with no UI attached

The job is =allow_failure: true=, so it did not block, but it reddened every
macOS pipeline. It does NOT reproduce on the Linux docker runners.

* Cause

The test asserted a false invariant. =CLAL-LOAD-ALDO-CONFIGURATION= is not a
UI-hook-gated builtin: its handler is

: (load-aldo-configuration-from (clautolisp.configuration:config-load-path "aldo"))

which reads =clautolisp/aldo.conf= from =$XDG_CONFIG_HOME= then
=$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS= (=clautolisp/configuration/source/xdg.lisp:65=). Its result
depends on the FILESYSTEM, not on whether a UI is attached. The no-UI test
(=%with-no-ui-hooks=, forcing the 7 UI hooks nil) had it in its list anyway;
that passed only incidentally, because the ephemeral Linux runners have no
=aldo.conf=. The macOS runner is *persistent* and carries a real
=~/.config/clautolisp/aldo.conf=, so the builtin correctly loaded it and
returned non-nil — failing an assertion that never belonged there. Same class
as the earlier red-master incident and the "test the shipped artefact on a
persistent host" lesson.

* Fix (2026-09-13)

=clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/tests/builtin-tests.lisp=:
- Removed =(clal-load-aldo-configuration)= from
  =CLAL-UI-AND-DEBUG-BUILTINS-RETURN-NIL-WITHOUT-A-UI= (it is not UI-gated).
- Added =CLAL-LOAD-ALDO-CONFIGURATION-RETURNS-NIL-WITH-NO-CONFIG-FILE=, which
  is hermetic: it stubs =clautolisp.configuration::config-getenv= to point
  =XDG_CONFIG_HOME= and =XDG_CONFIG_DIRS= at a fresh empty temp directory (nil
  would fall back to =~/.config=, which on a persistent host may hold a real
  file), so =config-load-path= finds nothing and the builtin must return nil.
  Coverage of the builtin is preserved (the coverage tool still sees the call);
  the core loader =load-aldo-configuration-from= keeps its existing hermetic
  save/load round-trip tests in =clal-extensions-tests.lisp=.

Verified with the full image: =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl= exits 0, the new
test passes, the invariant test still passes, no regressions.

* Acceptance criteria

- [X] The no-UI invariant test no longer depends on the runner's filesystem.
- [X] =clal-load-aldo-configuration= stays covered, hermetically.
- [X] Full =test-sbcl= green.
